    |
    = note: `i` comes from outside the program: whoever sends it chooses the value, so nothing the compiler can see says what it holds.
    = note: The prover cannot state `0 <= i < f.lines.len()` here: a part of it is not a whole number it reads.
    = help: Check it where it arrives, with a guard the program handles: `throw BadInput(i) if !(0 <= i && i < f.lines.len())`, or the early `return` that rejects it. After that line, the index is proved.
